window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["0a"]={"https://theconversation.com/can-the-police-monitor-a-suspects-brain-during-interrogation-a-new-report-issues-a-stark-warning-295555":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"b07dba1985b411240ceb279f3414d911ccd72be017825dbaf3692c7547c448d9","read":"https://theconversation.com/can-the-police-monitor-a-suspects-brain-during-interrogation-a-new-report-issues-a-stark-warning-295555","bytes":181290,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Can the police monitor a suspect’s brain during interrogation? A new report issues a stark warning","by":[{"n":"Allan McCay","r":"Academic Fellow, School of Law, University of Sydney"},{"n":"David Hamer","r":"Professor of Evidence Law, University of Sydney"}],"pub":"2026-11-17T05:03:20Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["If you were arrested as a suspect in in a murder case, could the police make you put on a brain-monitoring device and then use evidence derived from it to try to convict you?"]},{"k":"p","s":["These questions are among many being examined in a ",["new report","https://www.unodc.org/res/justice-and-prison-reform/Neurotechnology_Assessment.pdf"]," on the use of neurotechnology in criminal justice settings, jointly published by INTERPOL and the United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime this month."]},{"k":"h","s":["How does neurotechnology work?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Neurotechnology is an umbrella term for ",["emerging technologies","https://post.parliament.uk/neurotechnology-what-is-it-and-how-is-it-used/"]," that are able to read and decode information from the body’s neural system. These technologies range from cochlear implants to brain-computer interfaces, which can transfer a person’s thoughts to an external device."]},{"k":"p","s":["Advances in neurotechnology that is not implanted have increasingly raised ethical and legal concerns about usage in non-medical settings, such as police interrogations. In a ",["report","https://geneva-academy.ch/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Neurotechnology-Integrating-Human-Rights-in-Regulation-1.pdf"]," one of us (Allan McCay) co-authored last year, we argued neural devices had been insufficiently tested to determine whether they actually work in criminal justice settings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet, some police forces around the world, such as in ",["the United Arab Emirates","https://www.mediaoffice.ae/en/news/2023/September/13-09/Hamdan-bin-Mohammed-launches-Dubai-Police-Genome-Centre"]," and ",["India","https://www.science.org/content/article/indian-police-are-trying-read-minds-suspects-over-neuroscientists-objections"],", are already using the technology when interviewing suspects to determine if they have “ ",["guilty knowledge","https://geneva-academy.ch/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Neurotechnology-Integrating-Human-Rights-in-Regulation-1.pdf"],"” of a crime."]},{"k":"p","s":["Researchers say this technology differs from a traditional lie detection test because of the potential to reveal the “fingerprint” of knowledge within the brain."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, a device called an EEG headset can be placed on the head of a suspect who is then shown a photo of the crime scene. The device’s sensors can then detect neural activity associated with recognition. The claim is the suspect may involuntarily betray their guilty knowledge."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another technique employs ",["neural lie detectors","https://newsroom.haas.berkeley.edu/brain-scans-help-researchers-untangle-the-truth-about-lie-detection/"]," in suspect interrogations. These are purportedly able to detect brain activity associated with lying. There are no reports of police currently using this technology."]},{"k":"p","s":["The new report argues neither approach has been scientifically proven to be effective. And even if they are shown to work at some stage, the report expresses concerns about the possible infringement of people’s human rights. These include the right to privacy, the right against self-incrimination, and the right to freedom of thought. It says:"]},{"k":"p","s":["[…] early awareness, scientific rigour, legal clarity and institutional preparedness\" is needed to ensure that neurotechnological developments ‘strengthen, rather than undermine, the rule of law’."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["If a brain can be caught lying, should we admit that evidence to court? Here’s what legal experts think","https://theconversation.com/if-a-brain-can-be-caught-lying-should-we-admit-that-evidence-to-court-heres-what-legal-experts-think-80263"]]},{"k":"h","s":["A legal grey area"]},{"k":"p","s":["So, do police currently have the power to use these technologies? And, if they do, would the evidence be admissible in court?"]},{"k":"p","s":["These questions have sometimes been a source of contention in courts."]},{"k":"p","s":["In India, for instance, a 24-year-old student, Aditi Sharma, was ",["convicted of the murder of her ex-fiance","https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8249088/"],", in part using evidence derived from a Brain Electrical Oscillations Signature test. In 2010, the Indian Supreme Court ",["ruled that evidence","https://www.ijllr.com/post/speculative-evidence-and-constitutionalism-the-limits-of-neuroscience-in-indian-jurisprudence"]," from the involuntary use of the technology was inadmissible in court. However, police still reportedly ",["use it","https://theprint.in/ground-reports/police-used-brain-forensics-banned-as-court-evidence/2664275/"]," in their investigations."]},{"k":"p","s":["The admissibility of such evidence is untested in Australia and there are as yet no reports of police usage. However, it’s clear the laws are similarly not equipped to address the potential uses of this technology by police. The Australian Human Rights Commission has ",["recommended a moratorium","https://humanrights.gov.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0032/70988/2509-Neurotech-Report_FINAL_ACC-1.pdf"]," on its use pending a further review by the Australian Law Reform Commission."]},{"k":"p","s":["New South Wales, for instance, has a ",["Lie Detectors Act","https://legislation.nsw.gov.au/view/whole/html/inforce/current/act-1983-062"],", which makes it a criminal offence to use a lie detector, regardless of the suspect’s consent or judicial authorisation."]},{"k":"p","s":["This legislation was ",["aimed at polygraphs","https://nswlr.com.au/view/6-nswlr-278"]," measuring “stress or vibration in the voice” and “changes in the subject’s respiration, pulse, blood pressure or muscular activity”, but it would likely also prohibit neural lie detection tests. Other uses, such as neural detection of image recognition, would not be covered."]},{"k":"p","s":["The state’s ",["Crimes (Forensic Procedures) Act 2000","https://legislation.nsw.gov.au/view/whole/html/inforce/current/act-2000-059"]," gives the police powers to use certain newer forensic technologies, but it makes no mention of neural monitoring."]},{"k":"h","s":["Can evidence be admitted to court?"]},{"k":"p","s":["What if the police used the technology in their questioning anyway?"]},{"k":"p","s":["When it comes to the admissibility of such evidence in court, this would be determined in most states and territories by their version of ",["Australia’s Uniform Evidence Law","https://store.lexisnexis.com/en-au/products/uniform-evidence-in-australia-4th-edition.html"],". This framework is skewed towards making evidence available to the court. Lingering scepticism about the validity of neural monitoring methods may be ",["no obstacle","https://theconversation.com/junk-science-is-being-used-in-australian-courtrooms-and-wrongful-convictions-are-at-stake-231480"]," to its admissibility."]},{"k":"p","s":["And, in the absence of ",["violence","https://legislation.nsw.gov.au/view/html/inforce/current/act-1995-025#sec.84"]," in police interrogations, a trial judge would have ",["discretion","https://legislation.nsw.gov.au/view/html/inforce/current/act-1995-025#sec.138"]," to admit illegally obtained evidence. The seriousness of the offence and usefulness of the evidence would be weighed against the gravity of the police misconduct and whether the suspect’s ",["rights were infringed","https://www.ohchr.org/en/instruments-mechanisms/instruments/international-covenant-civil-and-political-rights"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["This all means that in some circumstances, neural evidence might find its way into an Australian court, and could be used against an accused."]},{"k":"h","s":["The way forward"]},{"k":"p","s":["The new report recommends states adopt clear, binding legal frameworks for the use of neurotechnology in law enforcement. The report specifically highlights potential uses that could violate a person’s human rights, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["compulsory or coercive neural lie detection, memory retrieval and guilty knowledge testing"]},{"k":"li","s":["the use of neurotechnology for interrogation, behavioural compliance or involuntary treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["The report also stresses that responsible use of neurotechnology by law enforcement must meet “robust, transparent and independently verifiable scientific standards”."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s clear more regulation and oversight is urgently needed. As the report states, there is a gap between what this technology promises and what it can reliably deliver. This means its use by police is premature and can potentially infringe on people’s rights."]}],"chars":5926},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/united-arab-emirates":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"a296902afea8628d813b7bb9a720078614e256bdc8336e958ada6264c3b2dcb3","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/united-arab-emirates","bytes":91277,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"United Arab Emirates travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-21T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-27T16:03:20+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The context in the Middle East remains deeply unpredictable and the risk of sudden escalation is high. Since conflict began in early 2026, Iran has stated its intention to target locations associated with the US and Israel, including, but not limited to, organisations, businesses, facilities, and institutions. There have been strikes and retaliatory attacks by Iran and others across the region against civilian and US military infrastructure."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals in, or planning to travel through, the Middle East should be prepared for possible flight cancellations, airspace closures, and travel disruptions. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["If you’re affected by a crisis abroad - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],". This includes guidance on “how to prepare for a crisis” with suggestions on what you might include in your emergency supplies and “what to do in a crisis”"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up to ",["FCDO Travel Advice email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/united-arab-emirates/email-signup"]]},{"k":"li","s":["follow advice from the local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information, including updates relating to airports and airspace which could close at short notice"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from areas around security or military facilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your departure plans under review, and ensure your travel documents are up to date"]},{"k":"li","s":["if advised to take shelter, stay indoors or find the nearest safe building or designated shelter. An interior stairwell or a room with as few external walls or windows as possible may provide additional protection. The greatest risk is from falling debris caused by intercepts, and you are safest inside a secure structure. Do not approach or touch any drone or missile fragments or unusual objects"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/united-arab-emirates/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the United Arab Emirates’ (UAE) rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in the UAE set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you contact the ",["UAE Embassy in the UK","https://www.mofa.gov.ae/en/missions/london"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter the UAE, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have a residence permit, your passport’s expiry date must be at least 3 months after the date you arrive in the UAE."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling through the UAE and not passing through immigration, your passport must have an expiry date at least 3 months after the date you will transit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can get a visitor or tourist visa issued free of charge when you arrive in the UAE. You do not need to apply in advance of travel. Your passport will be stamped with the visa as you go through immigration. It will be valid for up to 90 days over a 180-day period, which will begin from the date of first entry into the UAE. The stay can either be continuous or divided across multiple visits, provided the total duration does not exceed 90 days within the 180-day timeframe."]},{"k":"p","s":["You could face fines for exceeding your authorised stay which may accumulate for each day of overstay. If you want to extend your stay, contact:"]},{"k":"li","s":["for Dubai: ",["General Directorate of Residency and Foreigners Affairs","https://www.gdrfad.gov.ae/en"]]},{"k":"li","s":["for the rest of the UAE: ",["Federal Authority for Identity and Citizenship","https://icp.gov.ae/en/"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Living and working in the UAE"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you entered Dubai on a visit visa and want to work, you must get a probationary work permit valid for up to 3 months from the Ministry of Labour. If you are caught working on a visit visa, you could get a fine or a prison sentence, and you risk deportation."]},{"k":"p","s":["You risk arrest if you have lived or worked in the UAE and return when:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your previous visa is not in order - for example if you did not cancel your work visa"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have outstanding debts"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have an unresolved legal issue"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have any doubt about your status, get advice before returning from a ",["local lawyer","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=United%20Arab%20Emirates"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have questions about your visa’s validity or expiration date, or about how to work or stay in the UAE, contact UAE Immigration directly:"]},{"k":"li","s":["for Dubai: ",["General Directorate of Residency and Foreigners Affairs","https://www.gdrfad.gov.ae/en"]]},{"k":"li","s":["for the rest of the UAE: ",["Federal Authority for Identity and Citizenship","https://icp.gov.ae/en/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["from the UK: ",["UAE Embassy in the UK","https://www.mofaic.gov.ae/en/missions/london"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Residence visas"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you apply for a residence visa, you will have to take a blood test. If you test positive for any communicable diseases like HIV, hepatitis or tuberculosis, you may be detained and then deported, without appeal. Check the health and fitness requirements on the ",["UAE government portal","https://u.ae/en/information-and-services/health-and-fitness/health-conditions-for-uae-residence-visa"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["When applying for a UAE residence visa, it is common practice for your sponsor’s representative to give their details as the contact information on your application. When your residence visa is issued, update these details using ",["ICP Smart System services","https://smartservices.icp.gov.ae/echannels/web/client/guest/index.html#/serviceCards/714?administrativeRegionId=1"],". The UAE authorities use these details when they contact you."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Previous travel to Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have a valid or expired Israeli visa or stamp in your passport, you should not face difficulties entering the UAE as long as you do not plan to work. If you plan to work, further checks may be needed and there is a risk you may be refused entry."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a British-Israeli dual national and have any concerns about entering the UAE, contact the ",["UAE Embassy in the UK","https://www.mofa.gov.ae/en/missions/london"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Leaving the UAE"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are subject to a travel ban, involved in legal proceedings, have unpaid debt or are a child subject to a custody dispute, you may be prevented from leaving the UAE."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter the UAE, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s UAE guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/233/united-arab-emirates#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of UAE","https://u.ae/en/information-and-services/finance-and-investment/clearing-the-customs-and-paying-customs-duty"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to bring pork products or pornography into the UAE. Videos, books, and magazines may be subject to scrutiny and may be censored."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Weapons and related equipment"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have permission from UAE customs and the UAE Ministry of Defence to bring weapons and related equipment into the UAE, or to travel through the UAE with them, no matter how small the quantity or the purpose. This includes items such as ammunition, body protection items, cleaning kits and gun belts. If you intend to bring restricted items to the UAE, read the ",["UAE customs clearance portal","https://u.ae/en/information-and-services/finance-and-investment/clearing-the-customs-and-paying-customs-duty"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about what medications you can bring into the UAE. You will need approval from the UAE authorities to bring in medication that the UAE classes as narcotic, psychotropic, controlled or semi-controlled."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get approval in advance from the UAE Ministry of Health to bring medication. ",["Apply online to bring medication to the UAE","https://www.ede.gov.ae/ar/w/%D8%A5%D8%B5%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%A5%D8%B0%D9%86-%D8%A7%D8%B3%D8%AA%D9%8A%D8%B1%D8%A7%D8%AF-%D8%A3%D8%AF%D9%88%D9%8A%D8%A9-%D8%B4%D8%AE%D8%B5%D9%8A%D8%A9"],". The UAE authorities advise that applications are normally processed within 5 working days."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you arrive in the UAE without evidence of prior approval, the medication will not be allowed into the UAE, and you may be prosecuted. For information on controlled medicines or the process for obtaining permission, contact the UAE Ministry of Health. Email info@moh.gov.ae or telephone +971 800 11111."]},{"k":"p","s":["In all cases, there are limits on the amount of medication you can bring into the UAE legally. You can bring up to 3 months’ supply of medication as a visitor, reduced to one month’s supply if the medication is included in the list requiring approval."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to complete this approval process if you are only changing planes in a UAE airport and not passing through UAE immigration."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in the UAE"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in the United Arab Emirates (UAE)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists continue to issue statements threatening to carry out attacks in the Gulf region. These include references to attacks on western interests, including against UK citizens. Due to increasing regional tensions, Israeli and Jewish linked sites could be targets for terrorists in the UAE."]},{"k":"p","s":["Targets may include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["residential compounds"]},{"k":"li","s":["military sites"]},{"k":"li","s":["oil"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport"]},{"k":"li","s":["aviation interests"]},{"k":"li","s":["crowded places"]},{"k":"li","s":["restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels"]},{"k":"li","s":["beaches"]},{"k":"li","s":["shopping centres"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship"]},{"k":"p","s":["Maintain a high level of security awareness, particularly in public places and at public events."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take sensible precautions to protect yourself and your belongings."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when walking or travelling alone or at night, particularly if you are a woman. Use a reputable taxi company and do not accept lifts from strangers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sexual assault and rape are relatively rare but do happen. A man who is convicted of raping a woman will be given life imprisonment, and in some cases prosecutors may request the death penalty. However, UAE law places a high burden of proof on the victim to demonstrate that the sexual relations were not consensual, especially when the victim had consumed alcohol or where the alleged attacker was known to the victim. If the sexual relations are determined to have been consensual, either party may still face prosecution for the offence of sex outside marriage."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink and food spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not accept drinks from strangers or leave your drink unattended. Criminals can spike drinks and assault or rob you."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Property scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to buy property in the UAE, get appropriate professional advice as you would in the UK. FCDO has a ",["list of lawyers for Abu Dhabi and Dubai","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=United%20Arab%20Emirates"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["The UAE is a Muslim country. Respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions. Make sure your actions do not cause offence, especially during the holy month of Ramadan or if you visit religious areas. There may be serious penalties for doing something that might not be illegal in the UK but is in the UAE."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Your passport"]},{"k":"p","s":["UAE employers may ask foreign employees to deposit their passports with the company as part of their terms and conditions of employment. This is illegal under UAE labour law."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is normal practice for hotels to take a photocopy of your passport or Emirates ID."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hotel regulations"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot stay in a hotel if you’re under 18 years old and not accompanied by an adult."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pedestrian crossings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Only cross roads using designated pedestrian crossings. It is illegal to cross in other places and you may face a fine or even imprisonment. Take care when crossing, as vehicles often do not stop at zebra crossings marked on the roads."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. During this time, it may cause offence if you:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out ",["how Ramadan is observed in the UAE","https://u.ae/en/information-and-services/public-holidays-and-religious-affairs/ramadan"]," or get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that driving may be erratic, particularly when people are trying to get home at dusk"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance - fasting can cause tiredness, particularly during the late afternoon and early evening"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dress modestly in public areas like shopping malls:"]},{"k":"li","s":["women should cover shoulders and knees, and underwear should not be visible"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid transparent clothing or any attire that features imagery or phrases that could potentially offend others"]},{"k":"li","s":["swimming attire should only be worn on beaches or at swimming pools"]},{"k":"li","s":["cross-dressing is illegal"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some venues, events or buildings may have specific dress codes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swearing and rude gestures"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to swear and make rude gestures, including online, as they are considered obscene acts. You could be jailed or deported. Take particular care when dealing with the police and other officials."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Showing affection in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Showing affection in public is frowned upon. You can be arrested for kissing in public."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual relationships outside marriage"]},{"k":"p","s":["Consensual sexual relationships between a man and woman outside marriage are generally legal if both are aged 18 or over. This includes extra-marital sexual relationships. However, if either person’s spouse or parent/guardian files a criminal complaint, both parties of an extra-marital consensual relationship can get a prison sentence of 6 months or longer."]},{"k":"p","s":["If a person aged 18 or over has a sexual relationship with a person aged 17 or under, they will be prosecuted for having a sexual relationship with a minor. If both people are aged 17 or under, they will both be prosecuted but punishment is likely to be limited to a caution, parental supervision, judicial supervision, professional training or psychiatric treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are unmarried and give birth to a child in the UAE, you will only be able to get a UAE birth certificate if:"]},{"k":"li","s":["both you and your partner get married"]},{"k":"li","s":["you and your partner provide a joint declaration, certified by a notary public, to acknowledge the child - further information is available from ",["the Ministry of Health and Prevention","https://www.ehs.gov.ae/en/services/services-directory/issue-of-a-birth-certificate"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you become pregnant outside of marriage, your medical insurance may not cover you. Consult your medical insurance provider before getting pregnant, or giving birth in the UAE."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Financial crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Financial crimes, including fraud and the non-payment of bills (including hotel bills) can often result in a prison sentence, a fine, or both. You could also have your bank accounts and other assets frozen."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are arrested for a financial crime and are not resident in the UAE, it is likely you will not be allowed bail. If you are convicted, you may have to stay in prison until the debt is paid or waived, and you’ve served your full sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drinking or possessing alcohol is illegal in the Emirate of Sharjah, 30km north of Dubai."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to drink or be under the influence of alcohol in a public place anywhere in the UAE. British nationals have been arrested and charged under this law, often in cases where they have come to the attention of the police for a related offence, such as disorderly or offensive behaviour."]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal age for purchasing and drinking alcohol is 21 in Abu Dhabi, Dubai and in all Northern Emirates except Sharjah, where drinking and having alcohol in your possession is illegal."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are resident in Dubai and want to buy alcohol to drink at home, you must get a liquor licence. Liquor licences are no longer required for residents in the other Emirates excluding Sharjah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Liquor licences are not required in Dubai to purchase and consume alcohol in licenced venues like hotel bars, restaurants, and pubs. However, a liquor licence is required for consuming alcohol in private places like homes or private parties. While this requirement might not be strictly enforced in private settings, it remains a legal requirement."]},{"k":"p","s":["Outside licensed venues, you can only buy alcohol with a liquor licence from the 2 official liquor distributors in Dubai, ",["MMI","https://retail.mmidubai.com/"]," and ",["African & Eastern","https://www.africaneastern.com/"],". Tourists can get a temporary liquor licence which is valid for one month, from either supplier. This licence is only for use in Dubai."]},{"k":"p","s":["Liquor licences are not required for non-residents in the other Emirates where alcohol is available. You can buy and drink alcohol in licensed venues, such as hotels, restaurants and clubs."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs penalties"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is zero tolerance for drugs-related offences."]},{"k":"p","s":["The penalties for trafficking, smuggling, using and possessing illegal drugs (including residual amounts) are severe. Sentences for drug trafficking can include the death penalty. Possession of even the smallest amount of illegal drugs, including cannabis, can lead to a minimum 3-month prison term or a fine of between 20,000 UAE dirham and 100,000 UAE dirham. The Emirati authorities count the presence of drugs in the blood stream as possession."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some ‘herbal highs’ and products containing cannabidiol (CBD) are illegal in the UAE."]},{"k":"p","s":["Possessing, concealing or making transactions with money from drugs-related offences is illegal. You could get a prison sentence and a fine."]},{"k":"p","s":["UAE airports have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items, including cannabis. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers. You can be arrested for carrying drugs, even residual amounts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some skincare products and e-cigarette refills may contain ingredients that are illegal in the UAE such as CBD oil. If you are found in possession of such products, they will be confiscated and you could face criminal charges. A list of narcotic, psychotropic and controlled drugs where this rule applies, allowed quantities and documents to be presented can be found on the ",["UAE Ministry of Health website","https://mohap.gov.ae/en/services/issue-of-permit-to-import-medicines-for-personal-use"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Fundraising and charitable acts"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fundraising and acts of charity are heavily regulated in the UAE. This includes online and social media activity. Check whether any of the activities you are planning to do in the UAE, or while travelling through the UAE, is illegal. Get legal advice if necessary."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking photos in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take photos of some government buildings and military installations. Hobbies like bird watching and plane spotting may be misunderstood, particularly near military sites, government buildings and airports."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not photograph people without their permission. Men have been arrested for photographing women on beaches."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Technical equipment"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may need a licence to use equipment like satellite phones, listening or recording devices, radio transmitters, powerful cameras or binoculars. Get advice from the ",["UAE Embassy in the UK","https://www.mofa.gov.ae/en/missions/london"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Media activity"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must apply for the appropriate permissions to carry out media activity, including the production, transmission or distribution of printed, digital, audio, video or visual information. Failure to do so could result in imprisonment and a substantial fine."]},{"k":"p","s":["Information about media activity and how to obtain the necessary permits can be accessed by registering on the ",["National Media Council website","https://uaemc.gov.ae/en/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal in the UAE, and same-sex marriages are not recognised."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UAE is in many respects a tolerant society and private life is respected. However, there have been reports of individuals being punished for same-sex sexual activity, particularly where there is any public element, or where the behaviour has caused offence. This applies both to foreign national residents and tourists."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rip currents can occur at any beach and can sweep even the strongest swimmer out to sea. Check for warning signs, especially red flags which mean that swimming is dangerous. Only swim from approved beaches where there are lifeguards and flags indicating it is safe to swim ."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Use only licensed taxis or other recognised forms of public transport, which includes apps like ‘Careem’, ‘Uber’ and Abu Dhabi Taxi. In Dubai authorised taxis are painted cream with different coloured roofs – taxis with pink roofs have female drivers. In Abu Dhabi taxis are painted silver/grey."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are special taxis for women and children, which can be hailed from the roadside or can be booked in advance."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in the UAE, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["UAE traffic portal","https://u.ae/en/information-and-services/justice-safety-and-the-law/road-safety"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in the UAE. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re applying for residence in the UAE, you can use your UK licence until your residence permit is issued, after which you’ll need to get a UAE driving licence from the traffic department."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are not always as disciplined as in the UK and there is a high rate of traffic accidents. Speeding is common, despite clearly signposted legal limits and widespread use of speed cameras."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rules of the road"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to drink and drive, no matter how small the amount, and your insurance is likely to be invalidated in the event of an accident."]},{"k":"p","s":["Police in the UAE have the power to impound your car for traffic violations that may be considered minor in the UK. They will charge a fee of 50,000 UAE dirham plus a traffic violation fine to release your car."]},{"k":"p","s":["Offensive gestures and bad language directed at other drivers can lead to fines, a jail sentence, and possibly deportation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Flashing headlights can mean a driver is coming through, rather than giving way to you."]},{"k":"p","s":["All drivers involved in an incident must stop as soon as it is safe to do so. If you are involved in a crash, follow the rules of the emirate in which you are travelling:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Abu Dhabi, if no one has been hurt and vehicle damage is minor, move your vehicle to the side of the road to avoid blocking traffic, otherwise do not move your vehicle"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Dubai, only move your vehicle if it is causing an obstruction to other motorists"]},{"k":"li","s":["in the other emirates, only move your car if the accident is minor and both parties agree who is responsible"]},{"k":"li","s":["in all cases, call the police – it is illegal to leave the scene of an accident before the police have arrived"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving in the desert"]},{"k":"p","s":["Excursions to the desert can be dangerous unless you’re in a properly equipped 4-wheel-drive vehicle. Always travel with other cars, take a supply of water and a mobile telephone. Leave a copy of your travel plans with relatives, friends or where you are staying."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you join a tour for driving in the desert or quad-biking, make sure you go with a reputable company with adequate health and safety procedures."]},{"k":"p","s":["Always check that such activities are covered by your insurance."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be careful when travelling by tourist boat. The safety of these vessels may not be up to UK standards. Make sure life jackets are available for all passengers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many areas of the Gulf are highly sensitive, including near maritime boundaries and the islands of Abu Musa and the Tunbs in the southern Gulf. The authorities have detained and inspected vessels entering these areas. Mariners should make careful enquiries with relevant local authorities before entering these waters."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should consider how regional tensions may affect your route. Vessels operating in the Gulf of Oman, Northern Arabian Sea, Gulf of Aden and Bab El Mandeb regions may be at increased risk of maritime attack."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy rain in the UAE can cause flooding. Check weather forecasts from ",["the National Centre of Meteorology","https://www.ncm.gov.ae/maps-radars/gcc-radars-network?lang=ar"],", and follow advice from the local authorities. Sources for up-to-date information include local radio and online media outlets ",["The National","https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/uae/"]," and ",["The Khaleej Times","https://www.khaleejtimes.com/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 998 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for the United Arab Emirates (UAE)","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/233/united-arab-emirates#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in the UAE","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/233/united-arab-emirates"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or purchased in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the UAE, some UK prescribed and over-the-counter medicines are considered controlled substances. You must get approval in advance from the UAE Ministry of Health to bring medication. ",["Apply online to bring medication to the UAE","https://www.ede.gov.ae/ar/w/%D8%A5%D8%B5%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%A5%D8%B0%D9%86-%D8%A7%D8%B3%D8%AA%D9%8A%D8%B1%D8%A7%D8%AF-%D8%A3%D8%AF%D9%88%D9%8A%D8%A9-%D8%B4%D8%AE%D8%B5%D9%8A%D8%A9"],". The UAE authorities advise that applications are processed within 5 working days."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in the UAE"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in the UAE","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/united-arab-emirates-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["Healthcare facilities in the UAE are similar to those in the UK, but you may be stopped from using them without travel insurance or without the means to pay medical fees. You may be prevented from leaving the UAE if you are unable to pay your medical bill. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in the UAE","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-the-united-arab-emirates#healthcare-in-uae"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in the United Arab Emirates (UAE)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 998"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 997"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 999"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=united%20arab%20emirates"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=united%20arab%20emirates"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=united%20arab%20emirates"]," in the UAE"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in the UAE","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-guidance-united-arab-emirates"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in the UAE","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/united-arab-emirates-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/united-arab-emirates/british-embassy-abu-dhabi"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/united-arab-emirates/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in the UAE","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-united-arab-emirates"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":28498,"change":"Updated information about regional tensions (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)"},"https://theconversation.com/el-salvador-is-exporting-the-bukele-model-to-haiti-but-the-gang-offensive-is-a-gamble-for-both-nations-296390":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"9f9e4a5bd233cf4e419e951ae0d06a46b4fda0bcac9228fca692af8e368daa0f","read":"https://theconversation.com/el-salvador-is-exporting-the-bukele-model-to-haiti-but-the-gang-offensive-is-a-gamble-for-both-nations-296390","bytes":193635,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"El Salvador is exporting the ‘Bukele model’ to Haiti – but the gang offensive is a gamble for both nations","by":[{"n":"Robert Muggah","r":"Richard von Weizsäcker Fellow na Bosch Academy e Co-fundador, Instituto Igarapé; Princeton University"}],"pub":"2026-11-11T23:58:06Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["On Nov. 10, 2026, El Salvador President Nayib Bukele ",["posted footage","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/10/salvadoran-troops-target-haitian-gang-leaving-20-dead"]," of attack helicopters firing on a compound near Haiti’s capital, Port-au-Prince."]},{"k":"p","s":["He had earlier ",["requested, via a social media post in Haitian Creole, the address","https://www.infobae.com/america/agencias/2026/11/10/la-casa-del-lider-de-la-pandilla-haitiana-400-mawozo-fue-destruida-segun-afirma-bukele/"]," of Wilson Joseph, leader of the 400 Mawozo gang, one of Haiti’s most powerful criminal organizations. Bukele subsequently claimed the operation, conducted with Haitian police, had ",["demolished Joseph’s residence","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cmvg2xdwnwezo"]," and gang headquarters. As many as ",["20 people were killed","https://www.aol.com/articles/haiti-police-salvadoran-troops-destroy-161358000.html"],", although Joseph was reportedly absent."]},{"k":"p","s":["The attack comes amid a flurry of anti-gang operations in Haiti. On Nov. 6, Mathias Saintil, head of the “Boston” gang in Cité Soleil, ",["was killed","https://ca.marketscreener.com/news/haiti-pm-says-gang-leader-mathias-saintil-dead-ce785fd2df89f527"]," in a drone strike by a Haitian special task force, prompting Prime Minister Alix Didier Fils-Aimé ",["to declare on the social media platform X","https://x.com/citoyendidier/status/2118853047925551366"]," “one less gang leader.” Erik Prince, founder of the private military firm Vectus Global, ",["responded","https://beta.lenouvelliste.com/article/273679/le-premier-ministre-fils-aime-annonce-la-mort-de-mathias-saintil-lun-des-chefs-de-gangs-de-viv-ansanm"],": “Nice shot.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["As an expert on ",["organized crime in Latin America and the Caribbean","https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=oSuc5tUAAAAJ&hl=en"],", I believe these operations mark both a dramatic escalation in Haiti’s fight against organized crime and the first overseas test of Bukele’s security model. The intervention is ",["drawing support","https://apnews.com/article/dominican-republic-abinader-salvador-haiti-gangs-troops-55c1bdb8c82fce3b5d49ad33e6d8c194"]," from some regional leaders and pro-Bukele networks, even as concerns grow over civilian casualties and whether military gains can translate into lasting security."]},{"k":"h","s":["Rescue mission or military offensive?"]},{"k":"p","s":["El Salvador already had a limited presence in Haiti as ",["one of six countries","https://press.un.org/en/2026/sc16482.doc.htm"]," contributing personnel to the United Nations-backed Gang Suppression Force, or GSF. The force was ",["authorized in 2025","https://docs.un.org/en/S/RES/2793(2025)"]," to help Haitian authorities reclaim cities and streets from violent gangs that control swathes of the impoverished nation. But it remains ",["severely understaffed","https://www.koreaherald.com/article/10860194"]," and has struggled to translate military operations into lasting territorial gains."]},{"k":"p","s":["Then, in an Oct. 18 gang ambush, four Salvadoran aviation technicians attached to the Gang Suppression Force ",["disappeared","https://www.reuters.com/business/aerospace-defense/four-salvadoran-air-force-members-missing-after-gang-ambush-haiti-2026-10-19/"],". Their burned vehicle ",["was recovered","https://apnews.com/article/haiti-el-salvador-gangs-bukele-0302160e058789506d72c9e2a6c1bfc9"],", but their fate remains uncertain."]},{"k":"p","s":["Either way, Bukele used the incident to justify expanding El Salvador’s military presence in Haiti. Within weeks he had ",["sent roughly 2,500 troops","https://apnews.com/article/haiti-gangs-el-salvador-bukele-filsaime-c0986699cb1d618aed28f406d5a6975d"],", along with armored vehicles and attack helicopters, in what he ",["initially called","https://www.local10.com/news/world/2026/10/21/bukele-says-military-operation-launched-to-rescue-salvadorans-held-by-gangs-in-haiti/"]," a rescue mission."]},{"k":"p","s":["They joined an already crowded battlefield. Haiti’s ",["police and army operate alongside the GSF","https://www.unmissions.org/en/unsoh/news/security-council-extends-gang-suppression-force-and-unsoh-mandates"],", authorized but not commanded by the United Nations. The Haitian task force involved in operations against Saintil also works with former Blackwater CEO Prince’s ",["Vectus Global","https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/us-officials-see-closer-ties-with-trump-ally-princes-security-firm-in-haiti-military-adviser-says-4804441"],", while vigilante groups patrol contested neighborhoods. Dozens of armed gangs associated with the gang coalition ",["Viv Ansanm","https://main.un.org/securitycouncil/en/content/viv-ansanm"]," control large parts of Port-au-Prince and operate beyond the capital."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Gang Suppression Force was authorized by the U.N. Security Council to ",["deploy up to 5,550 personnel","https://apnews.com/article/haiti-gangs-salvador-attack-military-dd5d4b617fc526d3f7d994274732fc7e"],", and it currently has roughly 2,000 on the ground. Most of the Salvadoran troops now in Haiti operate ",["outside its command","https://lenouvelliste.com/en/article/273523/un-the-vast-majority-of-salvadoran-troops-do-not-fall-under-the-frg"],". Haitian Prime Minister Fils-Aimé ",["insists that Haiti directs","https://apnews.com/article/fefbf2e40c1eef1cac6b0281cef961d0"]," the operations. Yet neither government has publicly disclosed the agreement specifying Salvadoran authority, rules of engagement or the deployment’s duration."]},{"k":"p","s":["Without a ",["published deployment agreement","https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2026/11/haiti-los-gobiernos-de-haiti-y-el-salvador-deben-garantizar-que-el-despliegue-militar-salvadoreno-respete-los-derechos-humanos/"],", the chain of command and rules for authorizing strikes remain unclear to the public."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite President Donald Trump’s support for Bukele, Secretary of State Marco Rubio ",["has distanced Washington","https://www.state.gov/releases/office-of-the-spokesman/2026/11/secretary-of-state-marco-rubio-remarks-to-the-press-21/"]," from the Salvadoran offensive, saying the U.S. was “not actively involved.” He ",["warned","https://www.axios.com/2026/11/10/el-salvador-state-department-haiti-gangs"]," that poor coordination could lead to friendly fire, while U.S. diplomats ",["formally protested","https://www.axios.com/2026/11/10/el-salvador-state-department-haiti-gangs"]," the risks to multinational troops and civilian personnel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Salvadoran authorities ",["dispute American allegations","https://www.axios.com/2026/11/10/el-salvador-state-department-haiti-gangs"]," that their gunfire struck the U.S. embassy and endangered multinational troops. They also ",["questioned the credibility","https://www.axios.com/2026/11/10/el-salvador-state-department-haiti-gangs"]," of the top U.S. diplomat in Haiti."]},{"k":"h","s":["Uncertain rules of engagement"]},{"k":"p","s":["Haiti’s security crisis is dire."]},{"k":"p","s":["In recent years, organized violence has reached levels associated with armed conflict. Almost ",["6,000 people","https://binuh.unmissions.org/en/binuh/communiques-de-presse/haiti-la-situation-des-droits-humains-reste-extremement-preoccupante-au"]," were killed in 2025, and ",["more than 4,000","https://efe.com/mundo/haiti-violencia-muertos-crisis-seguridad-tercer-trimestre-2026/"]," in the first nine months of 2026. Nearly ",["1.5 million Haitians have been displaced","https://dtm.iom.int/reports/haiti-report-internal-displacement-situation-round-14-august-2026"]," as of August 2026, and expanded offensives and gang reprisals could drive more from their homes."]},{"k":"p","s":["An independent ",["legal assessment","https://warwatch.ch/situations/non-international-armed-conflict-in-haiti/classification/"]," by the Geneva Academy of International Humanitarian Law and Human Rights classifies fighting between Haitian forces and the Viv Ansanm coalition as a noninternational armed conflict, a legal category that includes civil wars. The International Committee of the Red Cross has separately ",["warned of the risks to civilians","https://www.icrc.org/en/article/haiti-do-everything-possible-protect-population-effects-escalating-armed-violence"],", urging all sides to respect international law."]},{"k":"p","s":["The distinction matters because the rules on lethal force are different in war and policing. Both require civilians to be protected. But in an armed conflict, members of armed groups with combat roles can be targeted even when they pose no immediate threat. In a police operation, simply being suspected of gang membership is not enough to justify killing someone – lethal force is generally allowed only when necessary to protect lives."]},{"k":"p","s":["Of particular concern is the growing use of explosive drones and helicopter attacks in residential areas. At least ",["1,243 people were killed in 141 drone operations","https://www.hrw.org/news/2026/03/10/haiti-drone-strikes-put-residents-at-risk"]," between March 2025 and January 2026, including at least 60 people reportedly unconnected to gangs, 17 of them children. These operations predated the Salvadoran escalation but demonstrate the risks of using explosive weapons in populated areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the same time, overlapping mandates for foreign troops and private military contractors could complicate investigations into civilian casualties and allegations of unlawful attacks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Exporting the Bukele model"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some Haitians, exhausted by insecurity, welcome the international intervention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Crowds have ",["cheered Salvadoran soldiers","https://efe.com/mundo/2026-11-07/marchas-apoyo-bukele-haiti/"],", waving sticks and chanting Bukele’s name. A prominent Haitian human rights advocate ",["supported the deployment","https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/around-1000-soldiers-from-el-salvador-have-deployed-to-haiti-source-says-4976576"]," while warning that residents of gang-controlled neighborhoods are not necessarily gang members."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bukele promotes the offensive through ",["videos of troops and airstrikes","https://apnews.com/article/nayib-bukele-el-salvador-haiti-elections-war-on-gangs-un-rubio-democracy-5c8a5e284835778c31c9ff78c140afcd"]," amplified by Salvadoran officials and pro-government influencers. Messages in Haitian Creole and Spanish that ",["portray the strikes","https://www.laprensani.com/2026/11/10/internacionales/3810551-bukele-destruye-cuartel-pandillas-haiti"]," as victories against gangs closely resemble the government’s widely circulated footage of mass arrests and prison transfers in El Salvador."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under Bukele, who came to power in 2019, ",["homicides in El Salvador have plummeted","https://abc3340.com/news/nation-world/el-salvador-turnaround-from-murder-capital-to-safe-haven-nayib-bukele-cecot"],", ",["boosting a belief","https://www.project-syndicate.org/magazine/bukele-effect-in-latin-america-risks-to-replicating-el-salvador-model-by-robert-muggah-2026-03"]," in parts of South America and the Caribbean that an iron fist approach to gang violence is worth the associated cost to human rights. Indeed, security hardliners across Latin America have ",["pointed to","https://english.elpais.com/international/2023-03-17/bukele-intensifies-war-on-gangs-2000-more-inmates-transferred-to-biggest-prison-in-all-america.html?outputType=amp&utm"]," El Salvador’s falling homicide rate to justify similar crackdowns. Dominican President Luis Abinader has ",["endorsed the intervention","https://apnews.com/article/dominican-republic-abinader-salvador-haiti-gangs-troops-55c1bdb8c82fce3b5d49ad33e6d8c194"]," and confirmed logistical and intelligence cooperation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet the Salvadoran model has relied on emergency powers and mass incarceration. Around ",["1.7% of Salvadorans are imprisoned","https://www.hrw.org/news/2026/10/07/el-salvador-mass-trials-a-mockery-of-justice"]," – by far ",["the highest rate in the world","https://www.prisonstudies.org/world-prison-data/highest-lowest/highest-lowest-prison-population-rate?language_content_entity=en-gb"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Haiti presents greater operational challenges. According to the U.N. Office for Drugs and Crime, gangs hold extensive territory, ",["possess heavy weapons","https://www.unodc.org/unodc/frontpage/2024/April/haiti_-gangs-have-more-firepower-than-the-police.html"]," and maintain connections to political and commercial networks. Haitian institutions are weaker, and ",["children are widely recruited","https://childrenandarmedconflict.un.org/en/news/special-representative-secretary-general-children-and-armed-conflict-concludes-first-visit"]," into armed groups from a young age. Sustaining territorial gains would require functioning police and courts, along with protection for residents after foreign troops leave."]},{"k":"p","s":["The expanded Salvadoran presence in Haiti also carries political risks for both governments. Bukele is ",["seeking a third term","https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/el-salvador-presidents-party-nominates-bukele-seek-third-term-2026-07-13/"]," in February 2027, following ",["constitutional changes","https://www.asamblea.gob.sv/node/13645"]," that removed presidential term limits."]},{"k":"p","s":["Salvadoran military casualties could stir criticism at home and pressure him to escalate, particularly with the ",["four Salvadoran technicians","https://www.latintimes.com/salvadoran-technicians-missing-haiti-gang-ambush-601077"]," whose disappearance prompted the rescue mission still missing. For his part in Haiti, Fils-Aimé has publicly backed the offensive ahead of Haiti’s elections, ",["scheduled for","https://cephaiti.ht/elections-et-droits-de-lhomme-le-cep-prone-le-respect-des-droits-fondamentaux-lors-dun-atelier-consacre-aux-garanties-democratiques/"]," July and October 2027. Civilian casualties or failure to sustain gains could undermine his own government’s credibility."]},{"k":"h","s":["Beyond military operations"]},{"k":"p","s":["The deployment may foreshadow wider regional security arrangements."]},{"k":"p","s":["El Salvador belongs to the ",["U.S.-backed Shield of the Americas","https://www.govinfo.gov/app/details/DCPD-202600155"],", a coalition launched by Trump in March 2026 to ",["expand military cooperation","https://amp.dw.com/en/shield-of-the-americas-trump-launches-regional-coalition/a-76262744"]," against drug cartels and other transnational criminal groups."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Salvadoran operation in Haiti does not formally fall under that initiative, whose ",["15 signatories","https://www.forth.news/lists/state/CfK5nG2Hm6uuvGtfSJ793"]," have pledged closer security cooperation. But such partnerships could allow regional governments to deploy forces with American logistical support while limiting direct U.S. military involvement."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although the Salvadoran operation is the latest high-profile example, I have seen similar cycles working in Haiti since the 2000s. U.N. peacekeepers and Haitian police ",["cleared parts of Cité Soleil between 2007 and 2009","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20846354/"],", contributing to a decline in kidnappings but failing to deliver lasting security. The ",["U.N. mission later introduced cholera","https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2016/dec/01/haiti-cholera-outbreak-stain-on-reputation-un-says"]," following the 2010 earthquake, killing more than 9,000 people and prompting an eventual apology from the U.N."]},{"k":"p","s":["Gangs endure because their ",["economic networks survive","https://www.theglobeandmail.com/opinion/article-haitis-elites-should-be-held-accountable-for-backing-gangs/"]," military offensives. They profit from kidnappings and illicit trade while ",["controlling access","https://www.americasquarterly.org/article/flows-of-guns-and-money-are-dooming-haiti/"]," to key roads and markets. Removing leaders can ",["weaken organizations","https://my.rusi.org/resource/criminal-governance-politics-of-control-in-latin-america-and-the-caribbean.html"]," without ending these revenue streams."]},{"k":"p","s":["While the current Salvadoran offensive may deliver short-term security gains, sustaining them will depend on Haitian institutions maintaining control of recovered territory."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bukele’s intervention is now an overseas test of a security model with considerable political appeal. But its consequences will ultimately be measured by whether Haitians are safer when foreign forces depart."]}],"chars":9761},"https://theconversation.com/indian-gen-z-cockroach-protesters-aim-to-upend-assumptions-about-democracy-and-populism-in-modis-india-294730":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"10b7a78fea60a36404c1ac938f023e318a7ea3dc13656006fe5a94e148dc8339","read":"https://theconversation.com/indian-gen-z-cockroach-protesters-aim-to-upend-assumptions-about-democracy-and-populism-in-modis-india-294730","bytes":192449,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Indian Gen Z ‘cockroach’ protesters aim to upend assumptions about democracy – and populism – in Modi’s India","by":[{"n":"Amrita Basu","r":"Professor of Political Science, and Sexuality, Women's and Gender Studies, Amherst College"}],"pub":"2026-10-22T14:16:52Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Five months ",["after its founding","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/08/world/asia/india-cockroach-janta-party.html"],", India’s Cockroach Janta Party, known as the CJP, has revealed what youth-led democratic movements can achieve – and how hard they are to sustain."]},{"k":"p","s":["The movement was formed in May 2026 to protest the government’s cancellation of medical school entrance exams and after India’s Chief Justice Surya Kant likened unemployed youth to cockroaches. By July, the largely Gen Z movement had ",["scored an early victory","https://indianexpress.com/article/india/cjp-protest-dharmendra-pradhan-resigns-education-minister-10803141/"]," with the resignation of Education Minister Dharmendra Pradhan."]},{"k":"p","s":["The CJP has since moved on to a much larger political issue: The Election Commission’s reported ",["deletion of approximately 130 million names","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/14/india-protests-election-commission-gyanesh-kumar"]," from the voter rolls. Since Oct. 2, protesters have descended on the streets of Delhi, Mumbai and other cities demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar, halting the deletions pending an independent inquiry, and the restoration of the old electoral rolls before the next elections."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the process, the CJP has encountered ",["strong government resistance.","https://www.reuters.com/graphics/INDIA-POLITICS/POLICING/znvngnxmdpl/"],". Amid a crackdown on protests, two of the movement’s spokespersons – Ashutosh Ranka and Saurav Das – ",["were detained","https://www.reuters.com/world/india/indian-court-extends-custody-cockroach-movement-leaders-local-media-says-2026-10-19/"],", while Prime Minister Narendra Modi and his right-wing populist Bharatiya Janata Party, or BJP, have refused to bend on the voter roll issue – instead accusing protesters of undermining democracy."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nonetheless, as a ",["long-time scholar of Indian political parties and social movements","https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=ZsoF5nQAAAAJ&hl=en"],", I believe the CJP’s protests have revealed people’s deep-seated anxieties over democratic erosion in a country of nearly 1.5 billion. Through courage and acerbic wit, the CJP has done something that has eluded conventional opposition parties over the past 12 years: puncturing the ruling party’s ",["aura of invulnerability","https://time.com/article/2026/08/01/cockroaches-protests-gen-z-india-delhi-narendra-modi-prime-minister/"],". In doing so, I believe the protests have challenged the government’s view of who “the people” are, what democracy means, and who speaks for youth, women and the politically marginalized."]},{"k":"h","s":["Defining ‘democracy’ and ‘the people’"]},{"k":"p","s":["Modi ",["often describes","https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-10-13/modi-says-india-is-the-mother-of-democracy-video"]," India as the “Mother of Democracy,” a reference to its civilizational heritage and to Bharat Mata, the Hindu mother goddess. Democracy, he insists, is not a Western import but a native inheritance. The implication is meant to be reassuring: India has always been democratic and always will be."]},{"k":"p","s":["But some outside monitors disagree. Sweden’s V-Dem Institute classifies India as an “ ",["electoral autocracy","https://www.indiancentury.org/research-papers/inside-the-v-dem-rankings"],",” meaning that although it regularly holds multiparty elections, it fails basic democratic benchmarks such as legislative and judicial checks and balances and citizens’ active political participation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Judged by how the country treats dissent, the record is damning: using anti-terrorism laws ",["to jail activists without trial","https://www.dw.com/en/india-security-terrorism-laws-used-to-silence-dissent/a-75534044"],", barricading protest sites, ",["internet blackouts","https://www.techpolicy.press/indias-decentralized-system-of-internet-censorship/"]," and ",["police brutality","https://www.reuters.com/world/india/un-experts-urge-indian-authorities-cease-use-excessive-force-curb-protests-2026-10-20/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["By contrast, the CJP considers peaceful protest, along with upholding the country’s constitution, essential elements of democracy. Demonstrators regularly circulate images of ",["B. R. Ambedkar","https://www.constitutionofindia.net/members/b-r-ambedkar/"]," – the chief architect of the Indian constitution – on posters, in slogans and in songs. Like Ambedkar, 30-year-old CJP leader Abhijeet Dipke is a Dalit, or untouchable within the Hindu caste system."]},{"k":"p","s":["Critics argue that the BJP defines the nation through ",["Hindu civilizational identity","https://www.bjp.org/chapter-2"],", which is exclusionary because it rejects India’s rich Muslim historical traditions and casts doubt on the political loyalties of the country’s Muslims, who constitute about ",["14% of the population","https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2021/09/21/population-growth-and-religious-composition/"]," – 197 million people. By contrast, the CJP draws no line between insider and outsider by faith, caste or birth, and it defines community by shared commitments."]},{"k":"p","s":["The voter roll struggle shows what is at stake in the question. The Election Commission says the revision will remove duplicate entries, deceased voters ",["and noncitizens","https://indianexpress.com/article/express-exclusive/election-commission-sir-14-objections-gyanesh-kumar-sukhbir-singh-sandhu-vivek-joshi-10889737/"],". But critics worry that the burden of proof falls on voters. Consider how hard it is for poor Muslims, Dalits and migrant workers to produce decades-old birth, education and land certificates. Moreover, those whose names are struck from the electoral rolls fear being branded ",["illegal immigrants","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/14/india-protests-election-commission-gyanesh-kumar"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Cracks appear in BJP’s dominance"]},{"k":"p","s":["While the BJP had held the prime minister’s office before, Modi’s 2014 election marked a sea change in Indian politics, disrupting the Congress Party’s dominance."]},{"k":"p","s":["The BJP owed it electoral success in part to attracting young and first-time voters with promises of employment, economic growth and what is known in Hindi as “ ",["achhe din aane waale hain","https://www.reuters.com/article/world/us-politics/where-are-the-good-days-challenges-mount-for-indias-modi-idUSKCN1M10XG/"],",” or “good days are coming.” Since the BJP took office in 2014, the country has charted strong GDP growth, but the macroeconomic success ",["has been belied","https://www.bbc.com/news/world-asia-india-68823827"]," by ongoing and rampant inequality that falls especially hard on the poor and young."]},{"k":"p","s":["The BJP claims to have fulfilled some of its more targeted campaign promises, such as engaging in merit-based ",["public sector hiring","https://www.financialexpress.com/india-news/under-bjp-government-jobs-being-given-purely-on-merit-basis-says-haryana-cm-manohar-lal-khattar/1100415/"],". Yet 40% of Indian college graduates ",["under 25 are unemployed","https://thewire.in/labour/nearly-40-of-indian-graduates-under-the-age-of-25-are-unemployed-azim-premji-report"],". Paradoxically, the unemployment rate for youth who cannot read and write hovers around just 3.4%. For college graduates, who are the CJP’s main constituency, it is nearly nine times higher ",["at roughly 29%","https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-03-29/young-indians-more-likely-to-be-jobless-if-they-re-educated"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seizing on this building discontent, the CJP uses the slogan “Achhe Din” ironically, on posters and memes. Its manifesto opens: “If you are going to call us cockroaches, the least you can do is pay our rent.” It calls for making “lazy” – a code word for the unemployed – a protected political identity."]},{"k":"p","s":["Underlying the joke is a serious point: that stigmatization of the jobless offends millions of impoverished people, something critics note is protected in the dignity and equality guarantees of articles ",["21","https://indiankanoon.org/doc/1199182/"]," and ",["14","https://indiankanoon.org/doc/367586/"]," of the Constitution."]},{"k":"h","s":["Who speaks for women?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The BJP has gained women’s electoral support through a combination of targeted welfare schemes, support for increased women’s representation in legislatures and endless talk of women’s empowerment, or ",["“nari shakti","https://www.cambridge.org/core/services/aop-cambridge-core/content/view/5AC0841ABB6D7B5FFB85F680BB608F8B/S2977017326102126a.pdf/nari_shakti_womens_power_and_hindu_nationalism.pdf"],".”"]},{"k":"p","s":["However, masses of women protesters have challenged state-defined women’s empowerment. They stop police vans carrying detainees, scale barricades and criticize the prime minister."]},{"k":"p","s":["One of the most prominent among them is Neha Bora, a Ph.D. student and president of the left-wing All India Students’ Association, whose blunt messages to Modi has seen her profile skyrocket. Modi has said he has been subject to vulgar abuses by the protesters and was shocked by how “our daughters” could use such foul language, but he viewed them as “misdirected children” and was ready ",["to forgive them","https://www.telegraphindia.com/india/culture-shock-over-daughters-using-foul-language-but-ready-to-forgive-pm-modi-prnt/cid/2172744"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The throngs of women who are protesting express deep discontent with the government’s paternalism. They challenge its Hindu-inflected understanding of empowerment and insist on speaking for themselves rather than being spoken for. They express outrage at the government’s brutal response to their peaceful protests. They describe how the police have beaten and sexually harassed them, while anonymous self-styled guardians of religious morality engage in doxing, threats of rape and acid attacks, and circulate demeaning AI-generated images of them. For protesters, that record sits uneasily besides the prime minister’s denunciation of ",["violence against women","https://www.dw.com/en/india-independence-day-modi-condemns-violence-against-women/a-69945477"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["‘Cockroaches never die’"]},{"k":"p","s":["The CJP motto, “Cockroaches never die,” has wide resonance. Protesters have survived, but not escaped, violence, incarceration, internet blackouts and police blockades. The sunglass-wearing cockroach mascot makes a mockery of leader-centered nationalist branding."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent ",["youth-led uprisings in Bangladesh and Nepal","https://theconversation.com/what-gen-z-led-uprisings-across-asia-reveal-about-the-strengths-and-limitations-of-youth-protest-265706"]," have shown how quickly online mobilization can outrun official control. What distinguishes the CJP is that it pairs humor with legal and technical infrastructure. Its online portal ",["Saakshi vault","https://www.cockroachjantaparty.org/saakshi"],", which means “witness,” collects photos and videos of police violence that protesters upload; volunteer lawyers use these to issue complaints against officers."]},{"k":"p","s":["The CJP’s recent and remarkable successes do not mean that the movement is likely to disrupt the BJP’s hold on power in the next parliamentary elections in 2029. For now at least, the CJP is fairly concentrated in urban strongholds and would need to build organizational infrastructure and develop long-term demands."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, a generation that a government minister wrote off as lazy and expendable has exposed the cracks in the system that the chief justice defended. Whatever form it takes, the movement provides a vision and reminder of what democracy looks like."]}],"chars":8345}};
